BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 716.00 Tm (consume the same receivable. These properties remove check-then-write races within this controlled database path. Use) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 700.77 Tm (one local database on durable storage, not a network filesystem or independent copied databases. Set foreign keys on) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 685.55 Tm (every connection, retain FULL synchronous durability, and restrict write access to the service identity. The reference) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 670.32 Tm (makes no network submissions: it records an acknowledgement only after a documented external action. Where a) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 655.10 Tm (provider supports idempotency keys, reuse a stable claim identifier. Where it does not, an ambiguous timeout requires a) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 639.87 Tm (status inquiry and human resolution, never an automatic resend. A database transaction cannot make an unrelated) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 624.65 Tm (carrier system participate in an atomic commit.) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 609.42 Tm (The verification and escrow state machine starts at held, advances through verified, submitted, settled, and invoiced,) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 594.20 Tm (and allows documented voiding before settlement. Here escrow means an internal evidence hold, not possession of) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 578.97 Tm (client money. Submission requires a provider-qualified acknowledgement; settlement requires documentary proof that) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 563.75 Tm (the actual customer recovery equals the reviewed amount. A partial award stops the transition for controlled rework) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 548.52 Tm (rather than overstating fees. Invoicing records completed contractual performance and an unconditional fee right, then) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 533.30 Tm (debits fee receivables and credits operator revenue atomically. Bank receipts debit cash and credit those receivables) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 518.07 Tm (using an account-qualified bank transaction identifier. The minimal implementation allocates one bank transaction to) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 502.85 Tm (one claim; multi-invoice deposits need a dedicated allocation model before use. Reconciliation shows earned fees) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 487.62 Tm (minus allocated receipts equals remaining receivables for every claim and cohort. QA runs inside one read transaction,) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 472.40 Tm (avoiding inconsistent snapshots during concurrent writes. Structural checks supplement, rather than replace,) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 457.17 Tm (independent bank and source-document matching. Export monthly operator expenses into the accounting system) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 441.95 Tm (separately; do not infer owner profit from this revenue-only subledger. These supplied modules are reference source,) Tj ET
